## SLA

Composes, never reinvents: clocks are the service desk's own SlaTimerField (deadlineAt pre-adjusted, written only by commands); the window is FROZEN on at apply time (SlaWindowField); countdown and urgency maths is `cards/service-desk/utils/sla` — one source, so the card and a queue sort never disagree. Pauses are events, not booleans. `subject` is `linksTo(CardDef)`, so an SLA applies to any record, not only support cards.

```ts
import { Sla } from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/service-desk/sla';

@field sla = linksTo(() => Sla);
```

### Non-goals

Not the policy (SLA Policy owns targets); not ticket-level timers (Ticket carries its own SlaTimerFields — this card is for records that are not tickets, and for the ops roll-up).
